Logical: KGBpmnDefinitions
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN File"
Description: "One BPMN file as a unit -- the `bpmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the component that points at it and the subgraph that opens it name one resource. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-definitions."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* targetNamespace 0..1 uri "Target namespace" "The BPMN definitions' targetNamespace."
* exporter 0..1 string "Exporter" "The tool that wrote the file."
* exporterVersion 0..1 string "Exporter version" "The version of that tool."
* source 0..1 string "Source" "Where the node was read from: a repository path or URL."
* sha256 0..1 string "SHA-256" "Hash of the file the node was read from; pins the source."

Logical: KGBpmnProcess
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN Process"
Description: "One `bpmn:process`. Present as a node because a participant references it by processRef, and without it the pool-to-element attribution has nothing to travel through. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-process."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "The computable name: the CamelCase identifier a Canonical() reference matches on."
* isExecutable 0..1 boolean "Is executable" "The process's isExecutable attribute."

Logical: KGBpmnParticipant
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN Participant"
Description: "A pool: a role that owns part of the collaboration. The lifecycle BPMN has 8 and declares no laneSet at all, so the pool is the only unit of role assignment present and its @name is the sole link to a persona. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-participant."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "The computable name: the CamelCase identifier a Canonical() reference matches on."
* processRef 0..1 string "Process ref" "The id of the process the participant's pool holds."

Logical: KGBpmnTask
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN Task"
Description: "A task or sub-process. It is what a DMN usingTask href points at, what sequence flows connect, and what a DAK-level task entry describes. Sub-processes carry isSubProcess rather than getting a class of their own -- the lifecycle BPMN has exactly one. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-task."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "The computable name: the CamelCase identifier a Canonical() reference matches on."
* taskType 0..1 string "Task type" "The BPMN element type (userTask, serviceTask, businessRuleTask, subProcess, …)."
* isSubProcess 0..1 boolean "Is sub-process" "Whether the activity is a sub-process."
* parent 0..1 string "Parent" "The id of the sub-process that contains it, when nested."

Logical: KGBpmnGateway
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN Gateway"
Description: "A branch or merge. Included for connectivity rather than for a cross-model edge: a flow through a gateway with no node would point at nothing, and every reachability question over the process would break at the first decision point. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-gateway."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "The computable name: the CamelCase identifier a Canonical() reference matches on."
* gatewayType 0..1 string "Gateway type" "The BPMN gateway element type (exclusiveGateway, parallelGateway, …)."
* direction 0..1 code "Direction" "The gateway's gatewayDirection."
* direction from KGGatewayDirectionVS (required)

Logical: KGBpmnEvent
Title: "Knowledge graph L2-BPMN: BPMN Event"
Description: "A start or end event. Same connectivity argument as gateway, plus one of its own: entry and exit points are what make 'is this task reachable' and 'does this path terminate' answerable at all. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/bpmn-event."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* id 0..1 string "Id" "The identifier the source declares (an FSH instance id, a BPMN or DMN element id)."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "The computable name: the CamelCase identifier a Canonical() reference matches on."
* eventType 0..1 string "Event type" "The BPMN event element type (startEvent, endEvent, intermediateCatchEvent, …)."
